{
  "index": 12,
  "response": " To calculate the area of a triangle using the given side lengths (3 cm, 4 cm, and 5 cm), we can use Heron's formula for the area of a triangle:\n\n1. Calculate the semi-perimeter (s) of the triangle, which is half of the sum of the three sides:\n   s = (a + b + c) / 2\n   where a, b, and c are the lengths of the sides. In this case:\n   s = (3 cm + 4 cm + 5 cm) / 2 = 12 / 2 = 6 cm\n\n2. Calculate the area using Heron's formula:\n   Area = sqrt[s(s - a)(s - b)(s - c)]\n   where a, b, and c are the lengths of the sides:\n   Area = sqrt[6cm * (6cm - 3cm) * (6cm - 4cm) * (6cm - 5cm)] = sqrt[6cm * 3cm * 2cm * 1cm] = 9 square centimeters.\n\nSo, the area of the triangle is approximately 9 square centimeters.",
